        "department": null,
        "description": "Principles of Economics is an introductory and essential course for students across disciplines, offering foundational knowledge critical to understanding decision-making, markets, and economic systems. It lays foundations to understand the core concepts needed to analyse consumer behaviour, market dynamics, and policy impacts. Additionally, it has applications in areas like algorithmic trading, optimization, and data analysis, where understanding incentives and resource allocation is crucial. Topics will include, but are not limit to demand and supply, scarcity, externalities, consumer and producer theory, market structures the workings of financial markets. In addition, it introduces macroeconomics concepts like inflation, unemployment, and economic growth. The course is useful both independently, and as a stepping stone for advanced courses.",
